cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Octobox: An Online Toolbox for Corpus Linguistics"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Marchand
    given-names: Tim
repository-code: "https://github.com/timmarchand/octobox"
url: "https://timmarchand-octobox.share.connect.posit.cloud/"
abstract: >-
  Octobox is an R Shiny application for corpus analysis, bringing common
  corpus linguistics techniques (frequency, keyword/keyness, KWIC and
  collocation, dispersion, part-of-speech tagging, and lexical diversity)
  together in a single browser-based interface for researchers, teachers,
  and students.
keywords:
  - corpus linguistics
  - data-driven learning
  - R
  - Shiny
  - concordance
  - keyword analysis
